taylor: quick check — I pushed a small tf change to switch the ExternalSecret template to read from vault/data/apps/{{app}}/secrets instead of the old /secret/ path. also added `renewal: true` annotation and bumped `refreshInterval` to 15m. planning to roll in staging tomorrow morning, any objections?

nina: can you paste the exact patch? want to confirm svcacct perms and the role binding path.

taylor: sure — diff in the PR: 
```hcl
resource "kubernetes_manifest" "extsecret_app" {
  manifest = {
    apiVersion = "external-secrets.io/v1beta1"
    kind = "ExternalSecret"
    metadata = { name = "app-secrets" }
    spec = {
      refreshInterval = "15m"
      secretStoreRef = { name = "vault-cluster", kind = "ClusterSecretStore" }
      target = { name = "app-secrets", creationPolicy = "Owner" }
      data = [ { secretKey = "DB_URL", remoteRef = { key = "data/apps/myapp/secrets", property = "db/url" } } ]
      template = { type = "Opaque", metadata = { annotations = { "external-secrets.io/renewal" = "true" } } }
    }
  }
}
```

nina: looks fine. svcacct needs read on `secret/data/apps/*` and `auth/token/lookup-self`? rohan can confirm.

rohan: svcacct role should have `kv/get` on `secret/data/apps/*` and `sys/leases/renew` for rotation TTLs. the cluster policy we use is `kv-read-secrets + lease-renew`. make sure the mount path matches the CRD key (data/ vs secret/).

sam: small gotcha — ExternalSecrets operator expects `key` to be the full path under KV v2 but without the leading /, so `data/apps/myapp/secrets` is correct. if you use `secret/apps/...` operator will still try, but mapping breaks. :warning:

lina: pinging infra-bot for a quick lint and role check before staging rollout.

infra-bot: lint-check: passed (k8s manifest schema v1beta1). iam-policy-scan: warning — role `extsecret-access-myapp` grants `sys/leases/renew` but not `sys/leases/revoke` (ok for our flow). suggest documenting renewal window >= 1h.

taylor: thanks — I'm adding a note in the PR about the lease window. plan: merge after 09:00 PST smoke test, rollout to staging 09:30, monitor token refresh logs for 1h, then promote. any last blockers?

nina: one more ask — can we add a quick smoke pod that simulates 1 req/s to warm KV cache and validate TTL handling? I can add that to the helm chart.

rohan: +1 for smoke pod. also add a debug env var on the ExternalSecret controller in staging so we can see renew attempts in logs.

taylor: ok I'll add both and update the PR. thanks y'all :rocket:

sam: noted, will review the PR after you push the smoke pod changes.

lina: thanks — if infra-bot shows any other warnings, call it out here and we'll hold the rollout.

infra-bot: monitor-hook created: /infra/monitoring/playbooks/extsecret-rotation-check. threshold: token-renew-errors > 5 in 15m -> pager to #eng-oncall.
